{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund free doctors' letters for people eligible for free prescriptions",
        "additional_details": "Often the fees for doctors' letters can cause a barrier or create anxiety for vulnerable individuals. We feel that receiving further proof of health conditions for important reasoning, such as to gain emergency housing, should not come at a cost.\r\n \r\nWe believe that the free prescription system is in place for a reason to make health care more accessible for vulnerable individuals. Therefore, funding doctors' letters for such people seems appropriate and fair.",
        "background": "The Government should fund the provision of doctors' letters for those who are eligible for free prescriptions. We believe removing the need to pay a fee would make gaining proof of health needs more accessible for those on limited income.",
